top top::HexAsciiRom
vcd trace.vcd

# A ROM answers from constant data, so every check below runs at
# combinational speed: poke an address, let the wires settle with
# `advance`, and read the byte straight back. No clock edge ever
# needs to pass between the question and the answer.

# --- Phase 1: the decimal rows, '0' through '9'. ---
# The table opens on a tidy neighborhood: ten bytes at 0x30 and up.
poke top.nibble 0x0
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x30
poke top.nibble 0x1
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x31
poke top.nibble 0x2
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x32
poke top.nibble 0x3
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x33
poke top.nibble 0x4
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x34
poke top.nibble 0x5
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x35
poke top.nibble 0x6
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x36
poke top.nibble 0x7
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x37
poke top.nibble 0x8
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x38
poke top.nibble 0x9
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x39

# --- Phase 2: hold one address and make sure nothing drifts. ---
# Constant data does not wander: ask twice, get the same byte.
# (Two settles here, and more further down, also give the VCD
# flat, readable plateaus to debug against.)
poke top.nibble 0x5
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x35
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x35

# --- Phase 3: across the gap, to the letters. ---
# After '9' (0x39) the ASCII codes jump to 0x41 for 'A'. The
# table feels no seam, and neither should this sweep.
poke top.nibble 0xA
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x41
poke top.nibble 0xB
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x42
poke top.nibble 0xC
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x43
poke top.nibble 0xD
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x44
poke top.nibble 0xE
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x45
poke top.nibble 0xF
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x46

# --- Phase 4: spell with the whole table. ---
# The classic words a hex dump gets to say. Each character is one
# more read of the ROM, out of order, the way real callers would.
poke top.nibble 0xD
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x44
poke top.nibble 0xE
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x45
poke top.nibble 0xA
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x41
poke top.nibble 0xD
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x44
poke top.nibble 0x0
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x30
poke top.nibble 0xB
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x42
poke top.nibble 0xE
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x45
poke top.nibble 0xE
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x45
poke top.nibble 0xF
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x46

# --- Phase 5: both ends of the table, one more time. ---
# The addresses a bug is most likely to drop: the very first row
# and the very last.
poke top.nibble 0x0
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x30
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x30
poke top.nibble 0xF
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x46
advance
assert top.ascii == 0x46

exit
